From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:55:28 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] shelf-face-restock

A cart face built while Favorites or Recents restocks is dropped when
the cart at its index is no longer the cart it was built for. A restock
keeps the faces of carts still on the shelf, frees only the rest, and
keeps the selected cart selected (Recents still opens on its newest).
Stem lookups for the seated cart try the selected index first, so a
stem two platforms share resolves to the cart that was picked.
Reimplemented from marghost/slot_modded 88af60a (GPL-3.0),
https://github.com/marghost/slot_modded/commit/88af60a

(cherry picked from commit fb37347422f0a3218c571fa3b6f25dec1fbd3a65)
